STORM OF STRANDS (15s, 9:16, 30fps)

REFERENCE: Uploaded Image

STYLE
filigree-fiber creatures · flowing ribbon physics · hyper-real materials · iridescent silk · volumetric strand-vortex · dream-storm atmosphere

PHYSICS
• Strand bundles bend, whip, and ripple with simulated turbulence
• Fine fibers peel off and rejoin like fluid ribbons
• Color streams (yellow, red, teal) react to airflow
• Dustlike particles drift between strands
• Iridescent glints on curves and spirals
• Subtle body-breathing motion beneath the strands

CAMERA
Many shots · fast cuts · micro-movements · quick arcs · bold push-ins · no locked-off frames.
Always moving · expressive arcs · close-ups → wide reveals → tracking shots
Macro DOF for texture moments, then dramatic lens shifts.

SCENE BREAKDOWN (FAST CUTS)

S0 — Birth Swirl (0.0–2.0s)

Extreme close-ups of swirling strands forming the horse’s face. The ribbon-fibers of the horse flutter violently, like thousands of flexible strands snapping in turbulent wind. Micro-vibrations, iridescent sheen, visible depth.
Camera circles, macro detailing. Ribbons snap into place like magnetic silk.


S1 — Micro-Detail Burst (0.2–0.8s)

Macro close-up on the horse’s eye area; fibers ripple like liquid threads.

S2 — Mane Whip Pan (0.8–1.3s)

Fast lateral pan across the exploding, multicolored mane.

S3 — Face Lift Pulse (1.3–1.8s)

Close-up as the head rises slightly; strands peel back in fluid curls.

S4 — Crown Spiral (1.8–2.3s)

Orbit above the head: crown strands twist like tornado helices.

S5 — Neck Flow Tracking (2.3–3.0s)

Camera glides along the neck; ribbon layers flow like underwater silk.

S6 — Strand Vortex (3.0–3.8s)

Medium-wide: a swirling cyclone of loose fibers forms around the horse.

S7 — Shockwave Step (3.8–4.8s)

Hoof lands — a ripple of moving filament spreads across the ground.

S8 — Wind-Blast Turn (4.8–6.3s)

Horse sweeps its head to one side; filaments roar backward in a wind surge.
Camera swings around dynamically.

S9 — Launch Forward (6.3–8.3s)

It lunges into a gallop, creating long comet-like trails behind it.
Tracking shot from low angle.

S10 — High-Speed Cut Sequence (8.3–12.8s)

Three rapid segments:
• 8.3–9.3 — side sprint, strands streaming
• 9.3–10.8 — chase cam directly behind, debris swirling
• 10.8–12.8 — overhead swoop revealing a vast wake of ribbon-flow

S11 — Title Flash (12.8–15.0s)

Cut to dark background with drifting fiber dust.
Soft glowing serif letters emerge:

“STORM OF STRANDS”

A faint filament-wind hum closes the sequence.